      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JUST MY LUCK (7) produced a good effort when he worked but stuck on and finished fourth last start at Kilmore, beaten 5 metres. Drawn to enjoy an economical run and might sweat on the sprint lane. Can play a major role in the outcome. EVERY CENT COUNTS (1) finished fourth in both a heat and the final of the APG 2F Series at her only two starts to date. May have developed further with maturity and was readied with a trial. The ace draw should see a strong return. Stablemate FEAR THE MISSUS (2) was also last seen in the APG series, finishing at the tail in the 2CG Final four-and-a-half months ago. Well drawn and two nice trials suggest he is back in good order. ALCATRAZ MISS (8) must be considered after she came from a similar barrier and finished runner-up at Kilmore last week.",
